      "title": "Context — what this table shows",
      "type": "theory",
      "data": {
        "markdown": "## Solar-system reference\n\nEvery planet, sorted by distance from the Sun, with the figures most commonly cited in introductory astronomy:\n\n- **Mass** — in Earth masses ($M_\\oplus$).\n- **Radius** — in Earth radii ($R_\\oplus$).\n- **Distance** — semi-major axis in astronomical units (AU).\n- **Orbital period** — in Earth years.\n- **Moons** — known natural satellites.\n- **Has rings** — boolean indicator.\n\nUse the column headers to sort, the filter row to narrow the dataset (try `Saturn` in *Name*, or `min: 5` in *Moons*), and the pagination controls if your viewport is small."
      }
    },
